A child is now fixing the review findings on PR #54's own branch: [R1 03: fix review findings](<t3-thread://v2/461d8aa0-9e53-4578-a3c9-db2468bbeda5/thread:delegated-task:command%3Amcp%3Ace7e5897-2acd-40d1-ad99-c84c0df69b1f%3Adelegate-task%3Aaa14b4d4-13d7-4bdd-b459-36d7d2022fca>). It covers:
- closing the creation claim, so a removed creator can't get admin back;
- falling back to the Organization picker when someone is removed from one Organization;
- logout returning 403 or 503 instead of 500, plus revoking the session in WorkOS;
- Unicode-safe email normalisation;
- the missing tests.

I'm still watching #54 and will merge after re-checking the new commits and seeing a green real-WorkOS deploy on `pr-54`. The unauthenticated `/orgs` endpoints are now a blocking item on [R1 15](https://github.com/chrisdoc/surveybeat-next/issues/49), along with creating the WorkOS `admin` role in Production.

Three things to know:

1. **Your main checkout has someone else's work in it.** It has uncommitted WorkOS AuthKit changes on a branch called `feat/add-workos-authkit`. That isn't from this session. It may come from the `workos install` or `workos setup` you ran. R1 03 builds sign-in itself, so that branch would conflict with it. I haven't touched it, but you'll probably want to discard it.
2. **The R1 03 child created a WorkOS `admin` role on SurveyBeat Staging**, which had only `member`, because the creator's membership needs it.
3. **Still unconfirmed:** whether Email code, Google and Microsoft are enabled. They're in the WorkOS dashboard under SurveyBeat → Staging → Authentication. The `Drop` check after the state store upgrade is also still open.

